s (cooperation, adaptability). So mixed.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Weaknesses: relatively weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. So strengths: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence (weather, computers). Concerns: interpersonal (nasty remarks) and memory for numbers (attention/accuracy). Could be problematic.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. So strengths: decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence. Concerns: communication, cooperation, adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Weaknesses: regarded as a know-it-all, hot temper. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: temperament, cooperation.\n\nWe need to compare. Which candidate best overall? All have some concerns. Perhaps Candidate D has strong technical and responsibility, but hot temper and know-it-all may affect crew cooperation. Candidate B has stress handling and conscientiousness but nasty remarks. Candidate C has good decision making but egocentric and communication issues. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but show-off and not open to new ideas.\n\nWhich is best? Might be Candidate D because strengths across many criteria: responsibility, concentration, problem solving, adaptability, and adequate response to unexpected events. Concerns: hot temper and know-it-all could affect crew cooperation, but maybe less severe than egocentric or nasty remarks? Hard to decide.\n\nWe could start by presenting an initial recommendation for Candidate D, citing strengths and acknowledging concerns, and ask others for missing info about temperament impact. Or we could ask another panel member for more info about Candidate D's hot temper incidents. Use tool to ask agent_1 or agent_3.\n\nWe need to ask a specific question: e.g., \"Can you provide any observed examples of Candidate D's hot temper affecting crew cooperation?\" That would help evaluate.\n\nThus first public message: state provisional recommendation for Candidate D, reference strengths, note concerns, ask for clarification.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
